WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:03.091
(fast-paced drumming music)

00:00:03.091 --> 00:00:03.926
[Man] What time is it?

00:00:03.926 --> 00:00:07.221
♪ This is the dawning
of the age of Aquarius ♪

00:00:07.221 --> 00:00:08.347
"Summer of Soul"

00:00:08.347 --> 00:00:11.808
is about the Harlem
Cultural Festival in 1969.

00:00:11.808 --> 00:00:14.436
With so many
greats of music in the day,

00:00:14.436 --> 00:00:17.439
Tony Lawrence and Hal
Tulchin came up with an idea

00:00:17.439 --> 00:00:20.359
that we need to throw
a beautiful soul festival

00:00:20.359 --> 00:00:24.446
to use music to heal
a community that's hurting.

00:00:24.446 --> 00:00:26.573
♪ Let the sun shine ♪

00:00:26.573 --> 00:00:29.701
And when it came time
to distributing,

00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:31.203
they couldn't find any takers.

00:00:31.203 --> 00:00:33.080
In fact, a counterpart festival

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:36.166
that happened about 10 days
later called Woodstock,

00:00:36.166 --> 00:00:39.336
pretty much got to define
an entire generation.

00:00:39.336 --> 00:00:41.129
We wanted progress.

00:00:41.129 --> 00:00:43.799
We're black people
and we should be proud of this.

00:00:44.967 --> 00:00:47.970
The day that we got
nominated for an Academy Award,

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:48.887
I was just flabbergasted

00:00:48.887 --> 00:00:51.390
because I did not go into
this project

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:54.559
thinking that I was
going to make something

00:00:54.559 --> 00:00:57.813
that would affect people
emotionally like this.

00:00:57.813 --> 00:01:00.482
Getting nominated
really isn't about me,

00:01:00.482 --> 00:01:03.277
it's about documenting
a moment in time

00:01:03.277 --> 00:01:05.028
and the world's gonna see it.

00:01:05.028 --> 00:01:08.156
When you see films about
the Civil Rights era,

00:01:08.156 --> 00:01:11.535
there's one slight area
that always gets overlooked,

00:01:11.535 --> 00:01:12.494
Black joy.

00:01:12.494 --> 00:01:14.621
Black joy humanizes us.

00:01:14.621 --> 00:01:18.208
And "Summer of Soul"
is just an awesome look

00:01:18.208 --> 00:01:20.335
at beautiful people having fun

00:01:20.335 --> 00:01:24.339
in a way that you've never
seen anyone from this era look.

00:01:24.339 --> 00:01:27.009
♪ Gonna let my hair down
in Harlem ♪

00:01:27.009 --> 00:01:30.000
♪ 125th Street,
now here I come ♪

